hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16124","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, he said: I saw Muhammad ibn Maslamah pursuing a woman with his gaze, so I said: You look at her while you are of the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah Almighty casts in the heart of a man a proposal to a woman, there is no harm in looking at her."
"16125","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Burdah, he said: I passed by al-Rabadhah, and there was a tent. So I said: Whose is this? It was said: Muhammad ibn Maslamah's. So I sought permission and entered upon him, and said: May Allah have mercy on you, you are in a place in this matter, so if you went out to the people and commanded and forbade. So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be fitnah and division and dissension, and when that happens, bring your sword to Uhud and strike with it its edge, and break your arrows, and cut your string, and sit in your house. And that has happened. And Yazid once said: Strike with it until you cut it, then sit in your house until a mistaken hand comes to you or Allah Almighty grants you health. And what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said has happened, and I did what he commanded me. Then he brought down a sword hung on the tent pole and drew it, and it was a sword of wood. So he said: I did what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me, and I took this to frighten the people with it."
"16126","Muammal narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Burdah, he said: We passed by al-Rabadhah, and there was a pitched tent, and he mentioned it. He said: There will be fitnah and division, so strike with your sword the edge of Uhud."
"16127","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, he said: We passed by al-Rabadhah, and there was a tent. So I said: Whose is this? And he mentioned the hadith."
